there's no limit to how large or complex it can become.

698
00:34:28,430 --> 00:34:30,490
或许它们已自我改组了
Or maybe they've reorganized themselves

699
00:34:30,600 --> 00:34:33,090
以至于它们能够在许多物种成员中
so that they can share the thinking load

700
00:34:33,200 --> 00:34:35,460
分享思想负担了
amongst many members of the species,

701
00:34:35,570 --> 00:34:37,490
好比是计算机的分布处理
like distributed processing with computers.

702
00:34:37,610 --> 00:34:39,730
我的意思是 外星人为什么要满足于
l mean,why should the aliens be content

703
00:34:39,840 --> 00:34:41,930
局限在刚好能够装进
to be stuck with a kind of intelligence

704
00:34:42,050 --> 00:34:44,140
它们头脑的那种智能呢？
that can fit inside their heads?

705
00:34:47,720 --> 00:34:49,740
外星进化
Alien evolution

706
00:34:49,850 --> 00:34:52,340
可以产生出充满生机的机器星球
could produce a living machine planet

707
00:34:52,460 --> 00:34:54,510
脉动着数十亿个外星人头脑
throbbing with the combined intelligence

708
00:34:54,620 --> 00:34:56,550
所组合起来的智慧
of billions of alien minds.

709
00:34:56,660 --> 00:35:01,180
如果如此发达的生命存在 那我们怎么会认出它呢？
lf such advanced life exists,how would we spot it?

710
00:35:01,300 --> 00:35:03,450
我们究竟该咋办呢？
And should we even want to?

711
00:35:03,570 --> 00:35:06,060
外星人会当朋友欢迎我们么
Will aliens welcome us as friends

712
00:35:06,170 --> 00:35:07,920
还是视我们为威胁呢？
or view us as threats?

713
00:35:08,040 --> 00:35:11,930
抑或视地球为征服之地呢？
Or perhaps see Earth as a world to conquer?

714
00:35:12,040 --> 00:35:14,330
我们搞不清楚外星人的模样
We wonder what aliens look like,

715
00:35:14,440 --> 00:35:16,730
但我们对它们的模样又是什么呢？
but what do we look like to them?

716
00:35:16,850 --> 00:35:20,440
这个女人已经将她自己放进了它们的头脑
This woman has put herself inside their heads,

717
00:35:20,550 --> 00:35:24,180
她认为她已经有了答案
and she believes she has the answer.

718
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:30,490
人类只要仰望夜空
As long as humans have looked up at the night sky,

719
00:35:30,610 --> 00:35:34,060
就想知道外面是否有什么或有谁
we have wondered whether something or someone out there

720
00:35:34,180 --> 00:35:36,400
在回看
is looking back.

721
00:35:37,100 --> 00:35:40,400
我们想知道外星人是何模样
We want to know what aliens look like.

722
00:35:40,510 --> 00:35:44,300
我们又是何模样对外星人的呢？
What do we look like to aliens?

723
00:35:44,410 --> 00:35:47,800
如果有智能生命在那里
lf there is intelligent life out there,

724
00:35:47,920 --> 00:35:51,880
地球是否貌似值得一游的地方呢？
does the Earth look like a place worth visiting?

725
00:35:51,990 --> 00:35:55,350
2008年5月29日
May 29,2008.

726
00:35:55,460 --> 00:35:58,550
太空3100万英里处
31 million miles out in space,

727
00:35:58,670 --> 00:36:01,360
一个科技发达种族的眼睛
the eyes of a technologically advanced race

728
00:36:01,470 --> 00:36:04,790
扫描我们的星球寻找生命的签名
scan our planet for the signatures of life.

729
00:36:04,910 --> 00:36:08,360
不是外星人 但这仍然是非同寻常的
Not aliens,but this was still a close encounter

730
00:36:08,480 --> 00:36:10,730
近距离接触
of an extraordinary kind.

731
00:36:10,850 --> 00:36:13,570
它是航天局的太空探测器 EPOXI
lt was the NASA space probe Epo xi.

732
00:36:13,680 --> 00:36:17,170
发送回彗星的特写
Sent out to get closeups of comets,

733
00:36:17,290 --> 00:36:20,440
EPOXI短暂将镜头对准了它的母星
Epo xi briefly turned its lens back to its mother planet.

734
00:36:20,560 --> 00:36:22,310
第一遭
And for the first time,

735
00:36:22,420 --> 00:36:25,790
我们看地球就如外星人可能看我们那样
we saw the Earth as aliens might see us.

736
00:36:34,600 --> 00:36:39,260
天体物理学家萨拉.西格是EPOXI小组的一员
Astrophysicist Sara Seager was part of the Epo xi team.

737
00:36:39,370 --> 00:36:41,630
萨拉平时研究日外行星
Sara normally studies ex oplanets,

738
00:36:41,740 --> 00:36:43,000
搜寻外星大气层
looking for clues

739
00:36:43,110 --> 00:36:45,570
和生态系统的线索
about alien atmospheres and ecosystems.

740
00:36:45,680 --> 00:36:48,600
EPOXI探测器给了她机会去发现
The Epo xi probe gave her the chance to find out

741
00:36:48,720 --> 00:36:52,640
地球给外星天文学家可能的模样
what Earth might look like to an alien astronomer.

742
00:36:52,750 --> 00:36:54,040
如果你假装你对地球一无所知
lf you pretend you know nothing about Earth,

743
00:36:54,160 --> 00:36:55,440
那你将如何去认识地球呢？
what could you learn about Earth?

744
00:36:55,560 --> 00:36:58,750
外星人可能会分辨出地球的自转速度
An alien would be able to pick out Earth's rotation rate.

745
00:36:58,860 --> 00:37:00,080
它们可能会注意
They would be able to notice

746
00:37:00,200 --> 00:37:02,650
我们具有极有差异的反射面 -
that we have surfaces of very different reflectivity --

747
00:37:02,760 --> 00:37:04,020
那是云层 陆地及海洋
that's cloud,land,and ocean.

748
00:37:04,130 --> 00:37:06,120
它们还能看到我们有天气
And they could also see that we have weather.

749
00:37:06,230 --> 00:37:07,820
它们会看到的变化
They would see variability

750
00:37:07,940 --> 00:37:10,730
与地球自转速度无关
that isn't related to the rotation rate of Earth.

751
00:37:10,840 --> 00:37:13,630
EPOXI所做的第二件事是观察地球的光谱 -
The second thing Epo xi did was look at a spectrum of Earth --

752
00:37:13,740 --> 00:37:14,900
那就是 取白光
that is,take the white light

753
00:37:15,010 --> 00:37:16,770
将其劈成各种颜色
and split it up into the different colors

754
00:37:16,880 --> 00:37:19,270
来检视是否有什么颜色不见了
and to check and see if any of those colors were missing.

755
00:37:19,380 --> 00:37:21,200
我们称其为光谱
We call that a spectrum.

756
00:37:21,320 --> 00:37:24,370
地球颜色的频谱
The spectrum of Earth's colors

757
00:37:24,490 --> 00:37:25,840
就像是一面旗帜
are like a flag

758
00:37:25,950 --> 00:37:28,410
宣布了我们星球上存在有生命
announcing the presence of life on our planet.

759
00:37:28,520 --> 00:37:31,450
大海之蓝 云层之白
The blue of the oceans,the white of the clouds,

760
00:37:31,560 --> 00:37:32,850
大地之绿
the green of the land

761
00:37:32,960 --> 00:37:36,750
全都是生机勃勃的生态系统的标记
are all markers of an active ecosystem.

762
00:37:36,870 --> 00:37:39,580
如果一个外星人从远处眺望我们
lf an alien is looking back at us from far away,

763
00:37:39,690 --> 00:37:40,700
外星人会看到
the aliens would see

764
00:37:40,810 --> 00:37:42,220
我们大气层里有氧
that we have o xygen in the atmosphere.

765
00:37:42,340 --> 00:37:45,130
事实上 我们的大气层里有20%的氧气量
ln fact,our atmosphere has 20% o xygen by volume.

766
00:37:45,240 --> 00:37:47,560
迷人之处就在于 没有生命
What's so fascinating is that,without life,

767
00:37:47,680 --> 00:37:51,430
我们的地球基本上就要少100亿倍的氧
our Earth would have basically 10 billion times less o xygen.

768
00:37:51,550 --> 00:37:53,970
这样一来 氧气就基本上在地球上不存在了
So,o xygen would be essentially non-existent on Earth.

769
00:37:54,080 --> 00:37:55,940
地球上的氧来源于生命
And o xygen on Earth is created by life,

770
00:37:56,050 --> 00:37:58,870
所以那些外星人就会知道如此大量的氧
so those aliens would know that o xygen in such large quantities

771
00:37:58,990 --> 00:38:00,340
不应该存在于我们的大气层里
should not be in our atmosphere

772
00:38:00,460 --> 00:38:02,640
除非源源不断来源于什么东西
unless it is being continually produced by something.

773
00:38:02,760 --> 00:38:05,350
我们从地球物理学知道没有什么
And nothing that we know of in geophysics

774
00:38:05,460 --> 00:38:07,080
能够产生出如此多的氧气
can produce so much o xygen.

775
00:38:07,200 --> 00:38:08,780
那就是为什么我们将其归属于生命
And that's why we attribute it to life.

776
00:38:08,900 --> 00:38:13,020
外星人可能看到我们的星球支持生命
Aliens might see that our planet supports life,

777
00:38:13,130 --> 00:38:15,320
但它们或许没有看到
but they might not see

778
00:38:15,440 --> 00:38:17,830
地球是科技先进的
that Earth is technologically advanced.

779
00:38:17,940 --> 00:38:20,200
它们得仔细观观察
They would have to look carefully

780
00:38:20,310 --> 00:38:23,100
进行检测 诸如大气污染
to detect things like atmospheric pollution

781
00:38:23,210 --> 00:38:26,300
或我们城市的热特征
or the heat signatures of our cities.

782
00:38:26,410 --> 00:38:28,200
读取我们星球以及
Reading the colors of our world

783
00:38:28,320 --> 00:38:31,540
宇宙间数以百万计的类似的其它星球的颜色
and the millions of others like it out in the Universe

784
00:38:31,650 --> 00:38:34,540
对先进的外星文明来说易如反掌
would be easy for an advanced alien civilization.

785
00:38:34,660 --> 00:38:38,410
不幸的是 这对我们来说还不是很容易
Unfortunately,it is not yet easy for us.

786
00:38:38,530 --> 00:38:40,580
找出日外行星
Spotting ex oplanets

787
00:38:40,700 --> 00:38:43,550
推动了目前科技的限制
pushes the limits of current technology.

788
00:38:43,670 --> 00:38:47,690
如果我们想看到颜色 我们就需要一套新的手段
lf we want to see colors,we need a new set of tools.

789
00:38:49,700 --> 00:38:51,960
天体物理学家迪米塔.萨瑟罗夫
Astrophysicist Dimitar Sasselov

790
00:38:52,070 --> 00:38:54,160
想做点那方面的事情
wants to do something about that.

791
00:38:54,280 --> 00:38:58,430
这些是小圆行星
These are little round planets.

792
00:38:58,550 --> 00:39:02,840
我要投下几颗来表示凌日行星
l'm gonna just drop a few on to show transiting planets.

793
00:39:02,950 --> 00:39:05,270
我猜有两颗凌日
l guess there's two transiting.

794
00:39:05,390 --> 00:39:09,950
迪米塔的太太希拉画的深太空场景
Dimitar's wife,Sheila,paints scenes of deep space

795
00:39:10,060 --> 00:39:15,250
灵感来自他对开普勒行星探测器的研究
inspired by his research on the Kepler planet-finding probe.

796
00:39:15,360 --> 00:39:19,420
这就是我们想用开普勒去探索的东西
This is the kind of thing we want to discover with Kepler.

797
00:39:19,530 --> 00:39:22,820
有凌日行星 有一个卫星围绕着它
A transiting planet,and there is a moon around it.

798
00:39:22,940 --> 00:39:24,260
那就太好了
That would be great.

799
00:39:24,370 --> 00:39:26,290
这就是
So,there it is.

800
00:39:26,410 --> 00:39:30,830
那就是载有生命的行星 - 就在这里
That's the planet with life on it -- right here.

801
00:39:30,950 --> 00:39:32,070
我们有个大问题
We have a big problem.

802
00:39:32,180 --> 00:39:35,700
这个挑战涉及到我们无法分开测量
This challenge relates to our inability to measure

803
00:39:35,820 --> 00:39:38,610
恒星与行星的颜色
the colors of the star or the planets separately

804
00:39:38,720 --> 00:39:40,640
到极高的精度
to very high precision.

805
00:39:40,760 --> 00:39:44,310
面临的是10到100倍的挑战
And the challenge is about the factor of 10 to 100

806
00:39:44,430 --> 00:39:47,020
超越了当前科技水平
beyond what current technology works.

807
00:39:47,130 --> 00:39:49,950
我们最大的障碍
The biggest barrier we have

808
00:39:50,060 --> 00:39:52,220
是观察其它行星颜色时
to seeing the colors of other planets

809
00:39:52,330 --> 00:39:55,160
每个摄影师都会遇到的情况 -
is something every photographer has run into --

810
00:39:55,270 --> 00:39:57,490
相机抖动
camera shake.

811
00:39:57,610 --> 00:39:59,460
如果你要拍摄黑暗中的图像
lf you take a picture in the dark,

812
00:39:59,570 --> 00:40:01,460
你就需要有尽可能多的光
you need as much light as possible,

813
00:40:01,580 --> 00:40:04,430
这就意味着你无法挪动相机
which means you can't move the camera

814
00:40:04,550 --> 00:40:06,470
即你会获得模糊的图像
or you'll get a blurry image.

815
00:40:06,580 --> 00:40:10,310
类地行星非常小 极其遥远
Earth-like planets are so small and so far away

816
00:40:10,420 --> 00:40:14,580
它们的图像只够得上数码相机单个像素的
that their images only fill one thousandth of a single pixel

817
00:40:14,690 --> 00:40:16,680
千分之一
of a digital camera.

818
00:40:16,790 --> 00:40:19,480
如果那个像素稍有移动
lf that pixel moves even slightly,

819
00:40:19,590 --> 00:40:22,620
相机抖动将会破坏相片
the camera shake will ruin the picture.

820
00:40:22,730 --> 00:40:26,620
但是你又如何能够保持一个像素完全静止
But how can you possibly keep one pixel perfectly still

821
00:40:26,730 --> 00:40:28,920
数日乃至数年
over the days and years it takes

822
00:40:29,040 --> 00:40:31,830
来跟踪遥远太空里的对象呢？
to track an object in distant space?

823
00:40:31,940 --> 00:40:35,930
迪米塔的解决方案是太空激光梳滤波器（Astro-comb）
Dimitar's solution is the astro-comb.

824
00:40:36,040 --> 00:40:38,870
它利用激光维持望远镜的相机传感器
lt uses lasers to keep a telescope's camera sensor

825
00:40:38,980 --> 00:40:43,270
在几十年间的精确校准
precisely calibrated over a period of decades.

826
00:40:43,380 --> 00:40:46,440
你这里所看到的astro-comb
The astro-comb that you see here

827
00:40:46,550 --> 00:40:48,640
是个技术突破
is the technological breakthrough

828
00:40:48,760 --> 00:40:51,010
用来弥补那个不足
which was needed to bridge that gap.

829
00:40:51,130 --> 00:40:54,550
一旦我们看到了其它星球的真正本色
When we see the true colors of other worlds,

830
00:40:54,660 --> 00:40:58,590
我们就将会知道在整个宇宙间生命在哪里
we will know where and how life is distributed

831
00:40:58,700 --> 00:41:00,990
又是如何分布的
across the Universe.

832
00:41:01,100 --> 00:41:05,510
我们寻求外星生命的下一个阶段就即将开始
And the next phase of our quest for alien life will begin.

833
00:41:06,370 --> 00:41:08,530
它将把我们带向何方？
Where will it take us?

834
00:41:08,640 --> 00:41:11,770
何种刺激的新世界将被我们发现呢？
What exciting,new worlds will we see?

835
00:41:11,880 --> 00:41:16,500
何种新的意想不到的生物会居住在上面呢？
What new and unexpected creatures might live on them?

836
00:41:16,620 --> 00:41:20,810
生物学家认为那里的生命可能看上去类似地球上的
Biologists think that life out there might look earth-like,

837
00:41:20,920 --> 00:41:24,180
但它看上去不会是人类
but it won't look human.

838
00:41:24,290 --> 00:41:28,420
外面有如此多的行星 生命有如此多的机会
With so many planets out there,so many chances at life,

839
00:41:28,530 --> 00:41:32,420
我们可能有类人的亲属在遥远的地球上
we could have human-like relatives on a far-away earth.

840
00:41:32,530 --> 00:41:33,660
类似我们这样的生物
Creatures like us,

841
00:41:33,770 --> 00:41:35,960
或许如我们这样急于了解
perhaps as anxious as we are to know

842
00:41:36,070 --> 00:41:38,060
它们在宇宙间是否是孤独的
if they are alone in the Universe.

843
00:41:38,170 --> 00:41:44,100
随着我们手段的改进 我们发现它们的机会也增大了
As our tools improve,so do our odds of finding them.

844
00:41:44,210 --> 00:41:47,440
显然我们已经进入了
lt is clear that we're in a new age

845
00:41:47,550 --> 00:41:49,470
探索与发现的新纪元
of exploration and discovery.

846
00:41:49,580 --> 00:41:51,270
500年来
lt hasn't been for 500 years

847
00:41:51,390 --> 00:41:53,780
人类一直试图寻找
that people have tried to discover planets

848
00:41:53,890 --> 00:41:54,940
围绕其它恒星的行星
around other stars.

849
00:41:55,060 --> 00:41:56,810
现在我们发现了它们
Now we have them.

850
00:41:56,920 --> 00:42:01,150
我们还有更多的探索 好事还在后头呢
We have much more to explore,and the best is yet to come.

851
00:42:01,260 --> 00:42:02,820
1000年后
1,000 years from now,

852
00:42:02,930 --> 00:42:05,250
人们回顾我们这代人时会问
when people look back at our generation and ask,

853
00:42:05,370 --> 00:42:07,820
最大的成就是什么？
"What are the biggest accomplishments?"

854
00:42:07,940 --> 00:42:10,630
我觉得这些人开展星际旅行
l like to think of these people making interstellar journeys

855
00:42:10,740 --> 00:42:12,090
回头一想
and looking back and thinking

856
00:42:12,210 --> 00:42:13,960
我们就是开始这一切的人
we were the ones who started it all.

857
00:42:14,080 --> 00:42:18,300
外星人究竟是何模样？
What do aliens look like?

858
00:42:18,410 --> 00:42:21,140
我们想象力的极限在哪里？
What are the limits of our imagination?

859
00:42:21,250 --> 00:42:23,340
外星人真正面目
The true face of an alien

860
00:42:23,450 --> 00:42:26,940
可能会无视我们的科学猜测
will probably defy our scientific speculations.

861
00:42:27,060 --> 00:42:29,510
但我们的努力不会白费
But our efforts won't be wasted,

862
00:42:29,620 --> 00:42:33,050
即使我们所得到的所有细节都是错误的
even if we do get all the details wrong.

863
00:42:33,160 --> 00:42:36,690
我们关于外星生命的永恒好奇
Our eternal intrigue about alien life

864
00:42:36,800 --> 00:42:38,890
我们对它的持久恐惧
and our persistent fear of it

865
00:42:39,000 --> 00:42:41,690
全都出自同一个源头 -
both rise from the same source --

866
00:42:41,800 --> 00:42:44,990
寻求了解
the quest to understand our place

867
00:42:45,110 --> 00:42:49,100
我们在宇宙的生命大家族里所处的位置
in the family of life-forms that populate the cosmos.

868
00:42:49,210 --> 00:42:51,130
知道了那个
Know that,

869
